      "notes": "netem loss plus jitter on the gateway WAN. Shares the one netem qdisc with WAN-LOSS and LATENCY, so never run them together. Mean delay equals the jitter, so the spread is real (netem has no negative delay). Reported loss moves in steps of 2.5 percent because the probe pools 40 pings. Both Internet Packet Loss and Internet Jitter change, so the correct indicator is the combined entry. A participant who names only one of them is scored wrong: decide the coding rule before the sessions.",
